WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.005
He was the communist hardliner

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:07.640
with a softer side.

00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:10.777
Jiang Zemin was also a shrewd

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:12.379
and cunning politician.

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:14.180
He rose to the pinnacle of power

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.015
after the massacre

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:15.915
of pro-democracy

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:17.117
demonstrators in Tiananmen

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:18.985
Square in 1989.

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:20.387
He didn't order the crackdown,

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:22.422
but was handpicked by the man wh

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.257
Supreme Leader Deng Xiaoping.

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:25.625
A year after the bloodshed,

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.961
Jiang Zemin told America's ABC N

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:30.363
it was, quote, much ado about no

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:31.831
At first,

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:32.699
he was written off

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:34.501
by most as a political lightweig

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:35.568
who wouldn't last.

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:37.470
He was known as the flower pot.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.572
Lots of decoration and no action

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:42.175
But history would prove them wro

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.277
Jiang Zemin has had many more su

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:45.979
and failures,

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:47.247
and he's surprised

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:49.049
many people with his staying pow

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:49.649
as leader.

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:51.151
He quoted the military

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:51.985
and was determined

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:53.386
to keep the communists in power

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:54.387
while pushing ahead

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:56.322
with economic reforms.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:57.190
He's definitely

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:59.192
not going to be remembered as

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:01.227
China's Gorbachev. He's not even

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.130
on an official U.S.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.565
visit in 1997.

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:08.435
Jiang was lauded by Wall Street

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:09.636
and chastised by

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:11.271
President Bill Clinton over huma

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:12.705
rights on this issue.

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:15.175
We believe the policy of the gov

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:17.677
is on the wrong side of history.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:18.978
But he never gave ground

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.480
on political reforms

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.181
and explained

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:23.483
why during a rare interview with

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:26.286
I do think that to require all c

00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:26.786
to adopt

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:28.321
the same model of democracy

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:31.591
would itself be undemocratic.

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:33.426
He was leader when Hong Kong was

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:35.261
back to the mainland,

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.297
when Beijing was awarded the Oly

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:39.099
and businesspeople were allowed

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:41.334
to become communists.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.903
In 2003, he retired as president

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:44.804
The year after that,

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.139
he gave up his last post

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:47.941
as China's military commander,

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.676
completing the first smooth

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:51.211
leadership transition ever

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:53.113
in communist China.

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:54.814
So I want to thank you

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.749
for accepting my resignation,

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:57.684
he said at the time.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:01:59.953
Jiang still exerted

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.054
political influence

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:02.956
behind the scenes for years,

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:04.724
including the selection of curre

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:06.392
Chinese leader Xi Jinping,

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.393
who secured a norm

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:10.530
busting third term as party head

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.565
Xi, China's most powerful leader

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:13.466
in decades,

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.768
has eviscerated political rivals

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.871
including those in Jang's factio

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:20.273
and rolled back much of the econ

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:21.307
and personal freedoms

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:23.376
enjoyed during the Jiang era

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:24.244
in retirement.

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:26.412
Jiang reportedly sang an aria

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.214
at Beijing's National Grand Thea

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:30.517
before it was officially opened 

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.621
for a man who once ruled

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:36.556
more than a billion people.

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:37.824
The performance was said

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.159
to be the fulfillment

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:42.061
